{"maxId":267,"entries":{"chapter-24-study-integrative-medicine-and-health|Chapter 24 Study: Integrative Medicine and Health":["u1"],"summary|Summary":["u2"],"copy|Integrative care combines conventional and complementary approaches; ask directly about use, stress, beliefs, support and supplements (p329-331).":["u3"],"copy|Weigh benefits against polypharmacy, product variability and drug–supplement interactions; disclosure is often incomplete (p331-332).":["u4"],"copy|Vitamin D has bone benefit in institutionalized older adults; cognitive and other benefits remain uncertain. Magnesium evidence varies by indication (p332).":["u5"],"copy|Fish oil: 1000–2000 mg/day EPA/DHA is discussed for potential cardiovascular benefit, but trials conflict; no convincing Alzheimer-treatment benefit (p332, p334).":["u6"],"copy|Coenzyme Q10: 100 mg three times daily improved outcomes in one moderate–severe reduced-EF heart-failure trial as an adjunct to standard treatment; well tolerated (p334).":["u7"],"copy|Ginkgo: 240 mg/day standardized extract may help selected cognitive symptoms; evidence conflicts. Use cautiously with bleeding disorders or anticoagulants (p334-335).":["u8"],"copy|Vitamin E does not prevent MCI progression; some high-dose meta-analyses suggest increased mortality (p335).":["u9"],"copy|SAM-e: 200–1600 mg/day in divided doses depending on indication/route; empty-stomach absorption and possible mania matter (p335-336).":["u11"],"copy|Melatonin: start 0.3–2 mg immediate release 1 hour before bed; long-term adverse-effect evidence is limited (p336).":["u12"],"copy|Valerian: 300–900 mg standardized extract before bed; effects may take weeks, studies conflict, and severe liver disease warrants caution (p336-337).":["u13"],"copy|Black cohosh: studied Remifemin 20 mg once or twice daily; heterogeneous evidence, uncertain long-term safety and caution when estrogen is contraindicated (p337).":["u14"],"copy|Saw palmetto: 160 mg twice daily; formulation-dependent, conflicting 